Session 291 summary — D-488 leg 7 ruling part 1b is implemented and building:

**Landed (0.11.505, srcversion `7BFD835EDA68D87A5C6D621`, clean rebuild, no new warnings, NOT yet deployed):** The rx strand detector no longer fabricates a cached tenure when it finds our own CAW holder bit on the platter with no in-core state. The old repair set `pag_dlm_cached = true` while the published authority epoch was still 0, so a local fast-path reclaim could adopt write authority with no epoch — every buffer that tenure logged would be refused by a foreign replayer. It now marks the AG `READOPT_PENDING` and the bast worker resolves the strand off the rx path: it re-reads the slot, and if the bit is still ours it goes through the real attested acquire, which performs sess290's verified P294 READOPT mint (fresh epoch through a real CAS, never the surrendered one), publishes it, and then releases through the ordinary drain pipeline so the peer's BAST is serviced normally. New probes: P295-RX-READOPT-MINTED / -GONE / -FAIL. The P243 no-authority probe now covers every writable-tenure entry path per the ruling: the two cached-reclaim arms fail closed on an epochless cached hint (drop it and re-mint via fresh attested acquire), and the two release_pending reclaim arms — unreachable today because only the unlock quarantine sets that flag while holding `demoting` — got detect-only probes rather than a blind behavior change.

